# Prettier formats only the files this list lets through: Markdown anywhere in
# the repo, and the TypeScript packages listed below. Everything else is
# ignored, so new file types are left alone until a rule below adds them.
#
# Prettier also skips everything in .gitignore (node_modules/, dist/, target/,
# .turbo/). A rule here cannot bring those back.

# Ignore every file. Directories stay visible, so the rules below can re-include
# files inside them.
*
!*/

# Markdown, anywhere in the repo.
!*.md

# The TypeScript packages.
!/fixed-number/ts/**
!/sol-tools/ts/**
!/reward-clearing/sol-programs/reward-clearing/ts/**
!/avm/sol-programs/linear-engine/ts/**
!/browser/**

# Markdown that another source owns. Formatting these files makes them differ
# from that source.

# The GitHub wiki. This folder must match the wiki exactly, and the Wiki check
# in CI fails when it does not. See docs/github-wiki/README.md.
/docs/github-wiki/content/

# Oracle fixtures that the Rust crate mayf-fixed-drivers-fixture-gen writes.
# `cargo test` fails when the file differs from the generator's output.
/fixed-number/ts/fixed-number-ts/test/fixtures/

# Agent skills installed from other repos and tracked in skills-lock.json.
# .claude/skills/ holds symlinks into .agents/skills/.
/.agents/skills/
/.claude/skills/
